# TEC API POC

This is the technical documentation for the TEC API proof of concept: a local sandbox for experimenting with CCD configuration and its effect on Manage Cases.

Use these pages for architecture, database ownership, and the ExUI Upload batch file navigation work. Content is the same material that previously lived under `docs/` in the repository.

## Contents

- [TEC decentralised CCD architecture](/ccd-architecture.html) — components, case types, create/read flows, and local CFTLib topology
- [CFTLib database layout](/cftlib-shared-database.html) — `datastore` vs `tec.ccd` vs TEC business tables
- [TEC PCN blockframes](/tec-pcn-blockframes.html) — grey-box wireframes for case tabs and Next steps journeys
- [ExUI primary navigation — Upload batch file](/exui-navigation.html) — local nav proxy and how to verify Upload batch file
- [ExUI Upload batch file proposal](/exui-manage-batches-plan.html) — architect proposal and acceptance criteria
- [Nesting demonstration](/nesting-demo/) — example multi-level sidebar from nested folders

## Run locally

Start the application and this documentation site together:

```bash
./gradlew bootWithCCD
```

Design docs preview: [http://localhost:4567](http://localhost:4567). See the repository README for the full local service list and clerk login.
